<h1>Redspace</h1>
<p>Redspace has been theorized since 2357, shortly after the proper utilization of Bluespace; a mirrored dimension to our own with a vastly different speed of light, allowing a ship to traverse into bluespace, rapidly and easily accelerate far past the speed of light in our universe, then slow and dip back into ours with a fraction of the energy. Redspace, would be the mathmatical opposite of this, where it would take exceedingly more energy to accelerate and reach the speed of light, leaving it sluggish and altered in its own energy.</p>

<p>However, despite countless efforts and researchers attempting, no scientifically provable incident of Redspace could ever be confirmed.
In 2483 a cargo freighter vanished inexplicably, only to show up hundreds of light-years off course, with the entire crew missing, and data corruption showed mathematical impossibilities on a failed bluespace jump, that could only possibly happen with Redspace... but this was insufficient for the scientific community at large.</p>

<p>As of 2568, Outpost-21, and Outpost-16 in a neighboring star system, are the only places with confirmed experiences... Outpost-21 being the only place where it's repeatable. But, nothing is majorly known about the dimension, and still considered a myth outside of the local sector.</p>
